---
/**
 * Birding hobby island: "you as a bird".
 *
 * Take or upload a selfie; the browser finds your facial landmarks with a
 * vendored MediaPipe model (runs locally, nothing is uploaded) and draws a
 * bird-person: your real face warped onto a bird's beak and feathers, with the
 * species, bill and plumage picked from your features and colors. Same selfie,
 * same bird; Shuffle tries another variant.
 *
 * All behaviour lives in @/lib/hobbies/birding, bound via [data-bird-*] hooks.
 * The client entry is an Astro module so it satisfies the strict CSP; the
 * heavy landmark model is dynamically imported on first use.
 *
 * NOTE: this is the only island with a bundled dependency (@mediapipe/tasks-vision)
 * and large vendored assets (public/birding/). See docs/hobbies.md.
 */
---

<section data-bird-root aria-label="Selfie to bird generator" class="not-prose">
  <p class="mb-4 max-w-[62ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-3">
    Take or upload a selfie and the page turns you into a bird-person: it keeps
    your real face and morphs it onto a bird's beak and feathers, blended to your
    own colours. Your photo is read on your device and never uploaded.
  </p>

  <div class="border border-rule bg-band p-4 sm:p-6">
    <!-- choose -->
    <div data-bird-choose class="flex flex-col items-center gap-4 py-6">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
        <button type="button" data-bird-camera class="btn btn-ink">Take a selfie</button>
        <button type="button" data-bird-upload class="btn">Upload a photo</button>
      </div>
      <input data-bird-file type="file" accept="image/*" class="hidden" />
      <input data-bird-capture type="file" accept="image/*" capture="user" class="hidden" />
    </div>

    <!-- camera -->
    <div data-bird-camera-view hidden class="flex flex-col items-center gap-4 py-2">
      <div class="overflow-hidden border border-rule bg-black">
        <!-- mirrored preview reads more naturally as a selfie -->
        <video data-bird-video playsinline muted class="block max-h-[60vh] w-auto" style="transform: scaleX(-1)"></video>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-3">
        <button type="button" data-bird-shoot class="btn btn-ink">Capture</button>
        <button type="button" data-bird-cancel class="btn">Cancel</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- busy -->
    <div data-bird-busy hidden class="flex flex-col items-center gap-3 py-12 text-sm text-ink-3">
      <div class="h-8 w-8 rounded-full border border-rule border-t-ink motion-safe:animate-spin" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <p>Drawing your bird...</p>
    </div>

    <!-- error -->
    <div data-bird-error hidden class="flex flex-col items-center gap-4 py-10 text-center">
      <p data-bird-error-msg class="max-w-sm text-sm text-ink"></p>
      <button type="button" data-bird-retry class="btn">Try again</button>
    </div>

    <!-- result -->
    <div data-bird-result hidden class="flex flex-col items-center gap-4 py-2">
      <div class="overflow-hidden border border-rule bg-paper">
        <canvas
          data-bird-canvas
          width="512"
          height="512"
          style="width: 384px; height: 384px; max-width: 82vw; max-height: 82vw"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Your selfie turned into a bird"></canvas>
      </div>
      <div data-bird-tags class="flex max-w-sm flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1"></div>
      <div class="flex gap-3">
        <button type="button" data-bird-download class="btn btn-ink">Download PNG</button>
        <button type="button" data-bird-shuffle class="btn">Shuffle</button>
        <button type="button" data-bird-again class="btn">Another selfie</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-prose text-center text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
    Your selfie is handled only on your own device, and it stays in your
    browser's memory just long enough to draw the bird. It is never uploaded or
    saved to a database, and the site owner never sees or stores it. The bird
    image leaves your device only if you choose to download it.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  /*
   * The view-switcher in birding.ts toggles the [hidden] attribute. Tailwind's
   * Preflight is disabled in this project (applyBaseStyles: false), so there is
   * no base [hidden]{display:none} rule, and an author `.flex` utility would
   * otherwise beat the UA stylesheet and keep hidden views (including the busy
   * spinner) visible. Force it here so only the active view shows.
   */
  [data-bird-root] [hidden] {
    display: none !important;
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { initBirding } from '@/lib/hobbies/birding';

  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-bird-root]');
  if (root) initBirding(root);
</script>
